      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with that many plus one instead.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more effects attempt to modify how many counters would be put on a creature you control, you choose the order to apply those effects, no matter who controls the sources of those effects.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature is sacrificed as a cost to cast a spell or activate an ability, Mortician Beetle\u2019s ability resolves before that spell or ability.",
      "oracle_id": "dc5c4a38-a415-466a-a7ea-dc04eee7f691",
      "published_at": "2017-03-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Mortician Beetle\u2019s ability triggers whenever any player, including you, sacrifices a creature because some other spell, ability, or cost instructed the player to do so. Mortician Beetle itself doesn\u2019t allow you to sacrifice any creatures.",
